Alembic migrations for the EMC CMS backend.

The database URL is read from application settings (app/config.py), not from
alembic.ini, so migrations and the running application can never disagree
about the target database.

Common commands (run from backend/):

    alembic upgrade head              # apply all pending migrations
    alembic downgrade -1              # revert the most recent migration
    alembic current                   # show the applied revision
    alembic history --verbose         # show the full revision graph
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add members table"
    alembic upgrade head --sql        # emit SQL without connecting

Every revision must be verified against a clean database before it is
considered done (backend/AGENTS.md §20).
